      "writtenOn": "2017-12-20T01:42:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. ``default_limit`` should not be in the unique constraint. If so, there will be a case like:\nNova RegionOne instance 5\nNova RegionOne instance 10\n\nThis is incorrect.\n\n2. NULL could be in a unique constraint, but it has a problem here like:\nSuppose there are two line in tale already.\n\nNova RegionOne instance 5\nNova NULL      instance 10\n\nThen insert a new line \"Nova RegionOne instance 5\", DB will raise duplicated error.\nIf the new line is \"Nova NULL  instance 10\", everything goes well. But it will break our design goal.\n\nSo now I think we should give region_id a default value, such as \u0027\u0027, then the UniqueConstraint( \u0027service_id\u0027, \u0027region_id\u0027, \u0027resource_name\u0027) will be OK enough.",
      "parentUuid": "df87a7cf_006ab718",
